  "interpretation": [
    "Default partial-centroid/radius .5 preprocessing degrades airplane fidelity in all five seeds, with median paired p95 ratio 15.23.",
    "Centering alone degrades sofa fidelity in all five seeds, with median paired p95 ratio 7.51. Default combined centering/scaling has a much smaller effect (paired ratio 1.09).",
    "Scaling alone strongly degrades airplane fidelity (paired ratio 19.93). Centering and scale effects depend on the input and cannot be assumed additive.",
    "Our preprocessing is a demonstrated contributor to poor fidelity on public demos. The previous box result measures checkpoint plus preprocessing, not weights in isolation.",
    "This is not proof of absolute completion accuracy, general-object behavior, or a complete explanation of the box-trial failure.",
    "No production normalization fix has been validated: raw world-meter points do not share the canonical demo coordinates."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Two public demo samples only; five resampling seeds do not provide object-level population statistics.",
    "No complete public demo truth. Native predictions are a transformation reference, not an absolute accuracy oracle.",
    "Coordinates affect both learned inference and internal FPS, including its near-zero exclusion. These mechanisms were not separately isolated.",
    "Original upstream forward uses the previously validated Triton FPS/Torch gather adapter, not a compiled upstream CUDA binary.",
    "No new live Genesis, IMU, real sensor, grasp, or production Pilot integration was exercised."
